%description:

Tcp.fastopenLenientCookieValidation:strict -- host2 refuses the forged cookie.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "TCP Fast Open, server: accept each cookie of a valid length without a check;
false: accept only the cookie that this server gives the address of the client (RFC 7413
section 4.2.2)".

The classes: strict (false, the default) and lenient (true). The code:
TcpConnection::processFastOpenCookieBytes() accepts a cookie of a valid length without a check
with true; with false, only the cookie that the server gives the address of the client, and
for another cookie it gives a new one (RFC 7413 section 4.1.2). This test separates "strict" from the other value.

Host under test: host2, a Fast Open server; host1 is a Fast Open client (preconditions). host1 opens connection 1 at 0.1 s with Fast Open, which requests a cookie; at 0.5 s it opens
connection 2 with Fast Open and sends 500 bytes, which go on the SYN when host1 has a cookie
of host2. The tap
changes the first byte of the cookie on the SYN of connection 2: a forged cookie. Observation: level 1, host2 refuses the forged cookie: the SYN-ACK acknowledges only the SYN.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenLenientCookieValidation
%# class: strict
%# value: false
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenLenientCookieValidation
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpMutations.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpFastopenLenientCookieValidationStrict")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .mutate([](Packet *frame) { forgeFastOpenCookie(frame); })
                     .describe("the SYN of connection 2, with data: its cookie forged"))
        .act(action().at(0.1).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 1 with Fast Open"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie == "";
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 1: a cookie request")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16;
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 1: a cookie of 8 bytes")
                  .within(0.5))
        .act(action().at(0.5).run<TcpTestApp>("host1.app[1]", [](TcpTestApp& app) { app.socket().connect(app.addressOf("host2"), 1000, true); app.sendData(app.socket(), 500); })
                 .describe("host1 opens connection 2 with Fast Open, and sends 500 bytes"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .capture("isn2", "tcp.sequenceNo")
                  .first()
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      std::string cookie = tcpFastOpenCookieOf(context.event.packet);
                      return cookie.size() == 16;
                  })
                  .describe("the SYN of connection 2, with 500 bytes and the cookie")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == true")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("tcp.ackNo == {isn2} + 1")
             .describe("the SYN-ACK of connection 2 acknowledges only the SYN")
             .within(0.5));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenLenientCookieValidationStrict compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenLenientCookieValidation = false    # the parameter under test
*.host2.tcp.fastopenServerEnabled = true
*.host1.tcp.fastopenClientEnabled = true
*.host1.numApps = 2
*.host1.app[*].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpFastopenLenientCookieValidationStrict: PASS
